diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 84cb54e..2d41086 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -94,3 +94,25 @@ controller_server:
       curvature_backward_dist: 0.3
       max_velocity_scaling_factor_rate: 0.9
 ```
+
+
+### Optional path-corner steering
+
+`FollowPath.use_path_corner_lookahead` defaults to `false`. When enabled, translation steering targets the first unreached bend greater than 22.5 degrees before the ordinary lookahead point. A bend within one local costmap cell is considered reached. Linear speed, curvature regulation, final approach, and angular regulation retain their ordinary lookahead calculations. This keeps the steering direction from skipping across a planned detour; it does not add moving-object prediction. The published lookahead point shows the steering target.
+
+A standalone regression replays two recorded C041 obstacle-detour paths and checks straight paths, duplicate vertices, reached turns, and short final segments:
+
+```bash
+c++ -std=c++17 -I include test/test_path_corner_lookahead.cpp -o /tmp/test_path_corner
+/tmp/test_path_corner
+```
+
+### Experimental collision checked lookahead
+
+`FollowPath.use_collision_checked_lookahead` defaults to `false`. It requires translation-only control and corner lookahead disabled. When enabled, it samples the actual robot-to-target straight segment at half-cell spacing on the local costmap, rejects costs >=253 including unknown/outside, and shortens the target along the current path if necessary. Target distance caps speed over transform tolerance plus three control periods. The costmap inflation footprint must represent the full physical swept body; this does not predict moving obstacle trajectories. C041 qualification is pending.
+
+### Experimental collision-aware omnidirectional DWB
+
+`pb_omni_pid_pursuit_controller::CollisionAwareOmniController` wraps installed DWB with velocity estimated by regression over the latest 0.15 seconds of the supplied localization poses. Velocity is expressed in the nonspinning command frame. The downstream sensor_scan_generation odometry twist uses wall-clock transform differences; this wrapper instead uses localization pose timestamps and the nonspinning command frame. Simulation truth is never used. It requires `max_vel_theta: 0.0`, with physical spin handled separately and covered by the costmap footprint. The ordinary RMUL 2027 profile passed the finite C052 matrix: one fresh fixed-obstacle batch (12/12), one-proxy head-on moving (3/3), original near-endpoint reconstruction (3/3), baseline route (8 checks), and both obstacle-removal recovery scenarios. This does not qualify the fast profile or arbitrary environments. See the parent project's scripts/rmul2027/reports/C052-RESULTS.zh-CN.md for evidence and limits.
+
+The wrapper keeps the original DWB obstacle critics and adds a hard full-spin circle check (radius 0.432883794 m) at every trajectory pose, including its first pose. GoalDist retains the original critic callbacks and scale, but uses a local reachable geodesic field over the same hard-safe cells. Positive edge costs rise smoothly from 1 to 2 within two cells of the hard boundary, encouraging clearance without blocking additional cells. It uses localization poses and costmaps; simulator truth is not a navigation input. ROS Humble DWB/Navfn 1.1.20 was used in C052.
